        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "496c7c63-fbd7-5822-9386-cbdf72a8f943",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cristiana Cucchi, Bazooka Girl\n- Companies: HI-NRG Attack\n- Products: Velfarre 2000, I Like Chopin\n- Concepts: eurobeat, Italo disco, C-Eurobeat\n\nFacts:\n- Italo disco is a pop music genre that originated in Italy and was mainly produced from the late 1970s to the late 1980s.\n- I Like Chopin is generally regarded as one of the most significant Italo disco tracks of the mid-1980s.\n- Bazooka Girl is the stage name of Cristiana Cucchi, whose Chinese name is 郑玉婷 and pinyin is Zhèngyùtíng.\n- Cristiana Cucchi is a eurobeat vocalist, and eurobeat originated from Italo disco.\n- Cristiana Cucchi is one of the most well-known names on HI-NRG Attack, an Italian record label.\n- Cristiana Cucchi’s speedy and energetic songs, especially the English Chinese New Year hit Velfarre 2000, have charmed many C-Eurobeat fans.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "011206c0-5532-5946-9b00-e560d7741a7f",
        "text": "Page: Cristiana Cucchi. Sentence: Bazooka Girl (Chinese: 火箭炮姑娘, Pinyin: Huǒjiànpào gūniang) (real name: Cristiana Cucchi, Chinese: 郑玉婷, Pinyin: Zhèngyùtíng) is a eurobeat (originating from Italo disco) vocalist and one of the most well-known names on \"HI-NRG Attack\", an Italian record label.\nPage: Cristiana Cucchi. Sentence: Her speedy and energetic songs, especially her hit, a Chinese New Year song in English called \"Velfarre 2000\", have charmed many C-Eurobeat fans.\nPage: Italo disco. Sentence: Italo disco (sometimes hyphenated, such as Italo-disco, subjected to varying capitalization, or abbreviated as Italo) is a genre of pop music which originated in Italy and was mainly produced from the late 1970s to the late 1980s.\nPage: I Like Chopin. Sentence: It is generally regarded as one of the most significant Italo disco tracks of the mid-1980s.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
